1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,660
A letter waited forty years to be read.

2
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:05,120
And it changed who her father was.

3
00:00:05,690 --> 00:00:07,620
After her grandmother Mary died,

4
00:00:08,030 --> 00:00:09,940
Sarah went to clean out the old house.

5
00:00:10,430 --> 00:00:12,180
In her grandmother's favorite book,

6
00:00:12,410 --> 00:00:13,610
she found a yellow envelope

7
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:16,700
with no stamp and one name on it.

8
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:19,820
To Mary, only when I'm gone.

9
00:00:20,610 --> 00:00:24,010
Inside, her great-grandmother wrote that the man Mary called

10
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:26,320
father was not her real father.

11
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:28,950
In the summer of nineteen fifty-one,

12
00:00:28,990 --> 00:00:31,420
Mary had met a soldier named Thomas.

13
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:34,820
He left for the war and never came back.

14
00:00:35,430 --> 00:00:36,840
Daniel knew the truth.

15
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:38,720
He married Mary anyway,

16
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:40,490
raised her daughter as his own,

17
00:00:40,530 --> 00:00:43,300
and asked that no one ever speak of it.

18
00:00:44,030 --> 00:00:46,980
Sarah sat at the kitchen table, holding the letter,

19
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:49,530
and finally understood her quiet grandfather.

20
00:00:49,570 --> 00:00:52,100
He had not hidden a lie.

21
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:54,200
He had kept a promise.

22
00:00:54,550 --> 00:00:59,060
And some truths wait forty years because love needs time.
